  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Protecting At-risk children Vulnerable to Exploitation (PAVE)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The goal of this project is to develop and strengthen systems for comprehensive care of survivors of OSEC in the National Capitol Region and Central Visayas of the Philippines over a 2-year period. Specifically, the PAVE project will support social workers and other stakeholders to identify OSEC victims; strengthen comprehensive service delivery for up to 144 child OSEC survivors with a focus on mental health care and legal services; and increase much needed shelter provisions for victims of OSEC.</narrative>
  </description>
